#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""HasH-Arch Software Centre  (hash-store)

A graphical package manager for HasH-Arch — browse a Discover-style app
catalogue, search, install, update and remove software, and add your own
repositories, all without touching the terminal.

Sources : official repos (pacman) + AUR (yay) + flatpak (removal). The app
          catalogue is built from AppStream metadata (as KDE Discover uses).
Privilege: transactions run through `yay` with a GRAPHICAL password prompt
          (sudo -A + SUDO_ASKPASS=ksshaskpass); a "Remember password" option
          authorises once per session. Editing repositories writes
          /etc/pacman.conf via pkexec (polkit). No terminal, ever.

Usage:
    hash-store                 launch the GUI (Discover catalogue)
    hash-store --updates       launch on the Updates page
    hash-store --sources       launch on the Sources/Repositories page
    hash-store backend <cmd>   headless JSON: updates|search <t>|installed|info <p>|catalog|storefront|repos
    hash-store _writeconf <f>  (internal, run via pkexec) install <f> as /etc/pacman.conf
"""
